 {q:'How should a museum present an uncomfortable local history? What should it emphasize, and what should visitors refuse to ignore?',chunks:[['downplay','downplay(s|ed|ing)?'],['divert attention from','divert(s|ed|ing)? attention from'],['avert one’s eyes from','avert(s|ed|ing)? (my|your|his|her|our|their|one\'s) (eyes|gaze) from'],['be at the forefront of','(is|are|was|were|be|been) at the forefront of']],model:'A museum should not downplay painful events or divert attention from the people affected by them. Visitors, in turn, should not avert their eyes from difficult evidence merely because it makes them uncomfortable. Historians and community members should be at the forefront of the interpretation, with room for more than one perspective. Labels can explain disagreement instead of presenting one smooth, official story. I would also include recorded testimony from local residents. That approach would make the exhibition harder to consume passively, but it would treat both the evidence and the audience with greater respect.'},
 {q:'Describe a place or group with a strong public image. Does that image match reality, and what happens to people who disrupt it?',chunks:[['pass sth off as','pass(es|ed|ing)? .{0,45} off as'],['align neatly with','align(s|ed|ing)? neatly with'],['be blessed with','(is|are|was|were|be|been) blessed with'],['send sb packing','send(s|ing)? .{0,45} packing|sent .{0,45} packing']],model:'Our town cannot pass a routine market off as a historic festival without criticism. The publicity does not always align neatly with the event’s modest origins, although the photographs make it look ancient and elaborate. We are blessed with committed volunteers, so the reality is often warmer than the image. Still, nobody should send a thoughtful critic packing simply for asking questions. A strong public image should invite honest discussion rather than prevent it. If the organizers acknowledged the recent origins, visitors might appreciate the community effort even more.'}
],
